<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Petru Rareș</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1487–<a href="/years/1546">1546</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Petru Rareș was Prince of Moldavia from 1527 to 1538 and again from 1541 to 1546, an illegitimate son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-the-great">Stephen the Great</a>. He intervened in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> and fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> over Pokuttya, but in 1538 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a> invaded, deposed him and annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bender-moldova">Tighina</a> and the southern steppe. He was a great patron of the painted monasteries of northern Moldavia, including Moldovița and Probota.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Later princes had less room: <b>Petru Rareș</b> lost his throne and the Tighina (Bender) region when Suleiman the Magnificent invaded in 1538, and Dimitrie Cantemir’s alliance with Peter the Great ended in the Russian defeat on the Pruth in 1711.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-moldavia">Principality of Moldavia · Military</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Hârlău, in what is now <a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suceava">Suceava</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=47.43,26.91&amp;year=1525" aria-label="Hârlău on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5179 500 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Petru Rareș"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5629 770h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5629 770h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=47.43,26.91&amp;year=1525">What was here in 1525? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
